# Vercel's Root Directory for this project is `web`, but the CLI uploads the whole
# directory it is invoked from -- so `vercel --prod` must run from the repo root, and
# everything outside web/ is dead weight in that upload. Without this file the upload
# is ~1.5 GB and fails outright on "File size limit exceeded (100 MB)" as soon as a
# release APK exists under mobile/android/app/build/outputs.
#
# Top-level entries are anchored with a leading slash on purpose. An unanchored
# `scripts/` would also match web/scripts/, which the build needs -- package.json
# runs `prebuild: node scripts/check-env-safety.mjs` from inside web/.

# Sibling apps -- not part of the web build
/mobile/
/doctors/

# Backend, docs and root-level tooling
/supabase/
/audit/
/docs/
/scripts/
/*.md
/*.mjs
/*.log
/dev.log

# Build outputs and caches (safe to match at any depth -- Vercel reinstalls/rebuilds)
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/.expo/
**/.gradle/
**/dist/

# Binaries
*.apk
*.aab
*.keystore
*.jks
